XImaging is a lightweight, multithreaded, open source image viewer and
browser for FreeBSD, Linux and other Unix like platforms running X11.

The application can be run in viewer or browser mode. The viewer displays
full size images and provides zooming, panning, rotation and other useful
functions. The browser searches a directory for known image file types
and displays them as thumbnails.

Most common raster image types are supported directly. An ImageMagick
filter provides support for additional formats such as GIF, PSD, SVG and
XCF.

The program is written in C, uses the Motif widget toolkit, and is
distributed under the MIT license.
